exports[`READMEs > site README includes the site's removal warnings 1`] = `
"# Loomination

Loomination is a free weaving design tool. It saves your drafts and settings here so they follow you to any computer you sign in on.

Website: https://www.loomination.org

## What Loomination saves here

- weaving drafts you have saved
- your loom profile
- warp plans and yarn calculations
- your yarn stash and AI-assistant notes

## Files in this folder

- \`state.json\`: Loomination's saved settings and items, as text.
- \`README.md\`: this file.
- Any other files are things Loomination saved for you.
- \`state.broken-<date>.json\`, if present, is a backup of a file Teather couldn't read. You can delete it.

## Managing this data

Go to https://teather.pages.dev/manage, sign in with this Google account and choose Loomination. There you can see each saved item,
edit or delete it, download files, or download everything.

## Removing it safely

1. On https://teather.pages.dev/manage, choose **Delete & disconnect** for Loomination. This signs you out of Loomination on every
   device and moves this folder to your Drive trash.
2. Or: sign out on Loomination first, then delete this folder.

If you delete this folder while you are still signed in on Loomination, the copy saved in your browser will be
uploaded again the next time you use it.

## Questions

About Loomination: https://www.loomination.org
About Teather: https://teather.pages.dev

_Teather writes this file and may update it. Your edits to it will be replaced._
"
